    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0209" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">130 Howe, Audrey Marie</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Canada (Boal) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1158</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-22">December 22,
                        1932</date>.<lb/>[Received January 3, 1933.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to instruction
                    No. 727 of October 7, 1932, concerning the question of the citizenship of Miss
                    Audrey M. Howe and to transmit herewith a copy of a note No. 156 of December the
                    16th, 1932, together with its enclosures, from the Secretary of State for
                    External Affairs,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d77-f1"/> in which it is stated that the
                    question of oaths to be taken by teachers is a matter within the jurisdiction of
                    the several provinces. The replies of certain of the provinces to an inquiry
                    from the Department of External Affairs are attached herewith.<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d77-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>In the case of Miss Audrey M. Howe, the Lieutenant-Governor of Alberta states
                    that she took the oath of allegiance in 1929. He adds: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Beyond this my Ministers have nothing further to add to the information
                            already furnished.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierre de L. Boal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
